
SYSTEM(3S)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           SYSTEM(3S)

NAME
     system - issue a shell command

SYNTAX
     system(string)
     char *string;

DESCRIPTION
     _S_y_s_t_e_m causes the _s_t_r_i_n_g to be given to _s_h(1) as input (as
     if the string had been typed as a command at a terminal).
     The current process waits until the shell has completed,
     then returns the exit status of the shell.

SEE ALSO
     execve(2), wait(2), exec(3), popen(3S), environ(5)

DIAGNOSTICS
     Exit status 127 indicates the shell couldn't be executed.

FILES
     /bin/sh

